dzn: Take flat inputs from the last vertex when a pipeline asks for it

Dozen advertises VK_EXT_provoking_vertex's provokingVertexLast and ignored
the mode: Direct3D 12 takes a flat input from the first vertex of a
primitive. ANGLE asks for the last vertex, as OpenGL ES uses it, so under
Venus every flat varying and integer fragment output of an Android app came
from the wrong vertex (dEQP-GLES3 fragment_out int/uint and
rasterization.flatshading: 558 failures on an RTX 4080 Laptop GPU under
WSL2, 8 with this change).

When a pipeline without geometry or tessellation stages uses
VK_PROVOKING_VERTEX_MODE_LAST_VERTEX_EXT and the device supports
barycentrics, its fragment shader reads flat inputs, of any type, at the
last vertex with attributeAtVertex, as Mesa's Direct3D 12 OpenGL driver does
for float inputs: vertex 2 of a triangle, 1 of a line, and 1 of the
(i + 1, i + 2, 0) triangles Dozen draws a fan as. Triangle strips keep the
first vertex, as Direct3D 12 numbers the vertices of their odd triangles
from the provoking one. The vertex is part of the shader cache keys.
nir_to_dxil gets an option to read integer inputs that way too; Mesa's
OpenGL driver does not set it.

